      "message": "\u003e sgs-\u003egroup_capacity instead of capacity_orig_of\n\nTo prevent migration between sibling SMT cpus when domain 0 is sibling level?\nGood point but I haven\u0027t thought about which way is better.  Will need discussion.  My gut feeling is we might be better preventing like you said though..\n\n\u003e sgs-\u003egroup_no_capacity instead of nr_running \u003c 2 and cpu_util_energy comparison\n\nstatic inline bool\ngroup_is_overloaded(struct lb_env *env, struct sg_lb_stats *sgs)\n{\n        if (sgs-\u003esum_nr_running \u003c\u003d sgs-\u003egroup_weight)\n                return false;\n\n-\u003e I agree using this portion will be right thing to do.\n\n        if ((sgs-\u003egroup_capacity * 100) \u003c\n                        (sgs-\u003egroup_util * env-\u003esd-\u003eimbalance_pct))\n                return true;\n\n-\u003e But worried about if this makes thing\u0027s too conservative because imbalance_pct is meant to be high enough make newly idle and busy load balancers conservative.\n\n        return false;\n}",
